{
  "prop|desc|, which Ask and Accept edits share (Hive tells them apart by the mode the session started in)": 1,
  "prop|desc|A limit's field with its window in minutes (300 is the 5-hour limit, 10080 the weekly one).": 1,
  "prop|desc|A limit's field with the percentage used.": 2,
  "prop|desc|A session error's message, in Copilot's session file, that means its sign-in was refused, when its type doesn't say so.": 1,
  "prop|desc|A session error's type, in Copilot's session file, that means its sign-in was refused or is missing (#309): Hive shows the agent signed out.": 1,
  "prop|desc|A turn's error, in Codex's session file, that means its sign-in was refused or has expired, when Codex doesn't mark the error itself (#309).": 1,
  "prop|desc|Claude Code's footer in the {} mode (\"{}\"). Hive reads an agent's permission mode from its footer (the mode found last on screen), and switches modes by pressing Shift+Tab until the footer shows the one wanted; wrong, Hive doesn't see the agent in {}, and can't switch to it without a restart.": 1,
  "prop|desc|Claude Code's line above its input when the last turn is done (\"✻ Worked for 12s · done 16:52\"). When Hive missed a turn's end, it takes this on screen to mean the agent is idle; wrong, it leaves such an agent's status unknown, with Mark idle.": 1,
  "prop|desc|Claude Code's note in its transcript when its safety classifier stops a response, and the notice it adds for the model (#606). Wrong, Hive misses such stops: no shield on the agent's pane, and Performance doesn't count them.": 1,
  "prop|desc|Claude Code's question after a safeguard stop, whether to switch models, told by its open dialog's choices in the lines it wrote last. Hive shows the agent waiting for you, and why, while it is open; wrong, the agent shows only \"Claude needs your permission\".": 1,
  "prop|desc|Claude Code's question before a folder's first session. Hive shows the agent as waiting for you while it is on screen.": 1,
  "prop|desc|Codex's Working line, drawn only while a turn runs. When Hive missed a turn's start or end, it takes this on screen to mean the agent is working; wrong, it can take a working agent for idle.": 1,
  "prop|desc|Codex's hint on the last line it draws while it is busy and queues what is typed. Hive waits for it to go before typing into Codex (a message, its /permissions menu at setup); wrong, what Hive types can be queued rather than run.": 1,
  "prop|desc|Codex's question before a folder's first session (in a Git repository). Hive shows the agent as waiting for you while it is on screen.": 1,
  "prop|desc|Copilot only says it has started with the first prompt, so Hive takes its footer on screen to mean it is ready.": 1,
  "prop|desc|Copilot's footer in the {} mode (\"{}\"){}. Hive reads an agent's mode from its footer (the mode found last on screen), and switches modes by pressing Shift+Tab until the footer shows the one wanted; wrong, Hive doesn't see the agent in that mode, and can't switch to it without a restart.": 1,
  "prop|desc|Copilot's question before a folder's first session. Hive shows the agent as waiting for you while it is on screen.": 1,
  "prop|desc|How long Claude Code waits for Hive to take one of its hooks (a turn starting or ending, a notification). Hive answers at once; raise it only if Hive's log shows hooks timing out on a slow machine.": 1,
  "prop|desc|How long Claude Code waits for Hive's answer before a tool runs (an edit waits for a file lock). If Hive doesn't answer in time, the tool goes ahead.": 1,
  "prop|desc|How long Codex lets one of Hive's tools run (its tool_timeout_sec for the hive server). Hive's waits stay a minute under it.": 1,
  "prop|desc|How long Codex waits for Hive to take one of its hooks. Codex itself holds the interrupt and session-end hooks to 3 s at most. Hive approves its hooks for Codex itself, so a change needs no review in Codex.": 1,
  "prop|desc|How long Codex waits for Hive's answer before a tool runs (an edit waits for a file lock). If Hive doesn't answer in time, the tool goes ahead.": 1,
  "prop|desc|How long Copilot waits for Hive to take one of its hooks.": 1,
  "prop|desc|How long Copilot waits for Hive's answer before a tool runs (an edit waits for a file lock). If Hive doesn't answer in time, the tool goes ahead.": 1,
  "prop|desc|How long the hive MCP server waits for Hive to answer one of its tools (a wait's own time comes on top). Raise it when a slow or very busy machine makes hive tools fail with \"Hive didn't reply within 300 s\" (#371).": 1,
  "prop|desc|How many agents a project can have (#562): {} unless you need more, up to {}. Each agent runs its own copy of its CLI, so more agents take more memory, and they all share your plans' usage limits. Lowering it removes no agents: a project with more just can't add another. Templates and the Agent API keep to it too.": 1,
  "prop|desc|How many card-loop lanes the Progress panel shows before its lanes scroll, until you drag the section's top edge (the drag is kept per workspace). A workspace that runs many lanes at once can set its own.": 1,
  "prop|desc|Show Help → Developer Console (Ctrl+Alt+J): what each CLI sends Hive, next to what Hive made of it.": 1,
  "prop|desc|Show the text in the developer console: prompts, replies, commands and tools' arguments, under a banner saying it is unredacted, and start each recording with its text box ticked. Tokens, API keys and sign-in details stay masked whatever this says; agents' hive_console stays redacted, and a recording with text is never attached to Copy Diagnostics.": 1,
  "prop|desc|The error a StopFailure hook names when Claude Code's sign-in was refused (expired, revoked, an invalid key): Hive shows the agent signed out and offers to carry on once it's renewed (#309). Any other error ends the turn as failed.": 1,
  "prop|desc|The field of Codex's token counts with a subscription's limits. Wrong, Hive shows no plan limits for Codex.": 1,
  "prop|desc|The label Codex's /permissions menu shows for its {} preset. Hive types the number beside it to give an agent the {} mode; wrong, Hive can't find it, and says so rather than choosing another.": 1,
  "prop|desc|The longest an agent's hive_wait_for_tasks call (without wake) waits before it answers. It has to stay under the CLIs' own tool timeouts, so Hive keeps it a minute below Codex's hive tool timeout whatever is set here.": 1,
  "prop|desc|The longest hive_wait_for_agents waits for agents to finish before it answers. Kept a minute below Codex's hive tool timeout, as card waits are.": 1,
  "prop|desc|The message of Copilot's ErrorOccurred hook that means a model call was refused for the sign-in: the turn ends signed out. Another error that ends the turn ends it as failed.": 1,
  "prop|desc|The plan limits' field for the 5-hour window.": 1,
  "prop|desc|The plan limits' field for the weekly window.": 1,
  "prop|desc|The status line's field with a subscription's limits (the 5-hour and weekly use the status bar shows). Wrong, Hive shows no plan limits for Claude Code.": 1,
  "prop|desc|The text Codex's empty input shows. Codex only says it has started with the first prompt, so Hive takes this text on screen to mean it is ready, and an input line showing only this to mean it is idle.": 1,
  "prop|desc|What Hive asks Codex to put in its terminal title (tui.terminal_title): its activity, which shows the busy spinner and \"Action Required\", and the project's name. Without activity, Hive can't tell from the title that Codex is working or needs you.": 1,
  "prop|desc|When Hive stops Copilot (Stop, Restart, closing a project or quitting), how long it gives Copilot to exit by itself after its Ctrl+C before killing it. Copilot writes the session's token totals only as it exits by itself: one killed first loses them. It took up to 2.4 s on a busy machine (#716); quitting Hive or closing a workspace waits up to this long, and a second more, for a Copilot that hangs.": 1,
